#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:29
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introdução"

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:31
msgid ""
"The idea of this proposal is to add native Unicode 3.0 support to Python in "
"a way that makes use of Unicode strings as simple as possible without "
"introducing too many pitfalls along the way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:35
msgid ""
"Since this goal is not easy to achieve -- strings being one of the most "
"fundamental objects in Python -- we expect this proposal to undergo some "
"significant refinements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:39
msgid ""
"Note that the current version of this proposal is still a bit unsorted due "
"to the many different aspects of the Unicode-Python integration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:43
msgid ""
"The latest version of this document is always available at: http://starship."
"python.net/~lemburg/unicode-proposal.txt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:46
msgid ""
"Older versions are available as: http://starship.python.net/~lemburg/unicode-"
"proposal-X.X.txt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:49
msgid ""
"[ed. note: new revisions should be made to this PEP document, while the "
"historical record previous to version 1.7 should be retrieved from MAL's "
"url, or Misc/unicode.txt]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:55
msgid "Conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:57
msgid "In examples we use u = Unicode object and s = Python string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:59
