#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:867
msgid "\"U\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:868
msgid "Check for Unicode object and return a pointer to it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:870
msgid "\"s\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:871
msgid ""
"For Unicode objects: return a pointer to the object's <defenc> buffer (which "
"uses the <default encoding>)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:874
msgid "\"s#\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:875
msgid ""
"Access to the default encoded version of the Unicode object (see Buffer "
"Interface); note that the length relates to the length of the default "
"encoded string rather than the Unicode object length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:880
msgid "\"t#\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:881
msgid "Same as \"s#\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:883
msgid "\"es\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:884
msgid ""
"Takes two parameters: encoding (``const char *``) and buffer (``char **``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:887 ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:901
msgid ""
"The input object is first coerced to Unicode in the usual way and then "
"encoded into a string using the given encoding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:891
msgid ""
"On output, a buffer of the needed size is allocated and returned through "
"``*buffer`` as NULL-terminated string.  The encoded may not contain embedded "
"NULL characters.  The caller is responsible for calling ``PyMem_Free()`` to "
"free the allocated ``*buffer`` after usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:897
msgid "\"es#\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:898
msgid ""
"Takes three parameters: encoding (``const char *``), buffer (``char **``) "
"and buffer_len (``int *``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:905
msgid ""
"If ``*buffer`` is non-NULL, ``*buffer_len`` must be set to "
"``sizeof(buffer)`` on input. Output is then copied to ``*buffer``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:908
msgid ""
"If ``*buffer`` is NULL, a buffer of the needed size is allocated and output "
"copied into it.  ``*buffer`` is then updated to point to the allocated "
"memory area.  The caller is responsible for calling ``PyMem_Free()`` to free "
"the allocated ``*buffer`` after usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:914
msgid ""
"In both cases ``*buffer_len`` is updated to the number of characters written "
"(excluding the trailing NULL-byte). The output buffer is assured to be NULL-"
"terminated."
msgstr ""

