#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:993
msgid "File/Stream Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:995
msgid ""
"Since file.write(object) and most other stream writers use the \"s#\" or "
"\"t#\" argument parsing marker for querying the data to write, the default "
"encoded string version of the Unicode object will be written to the streams "
"(see Buffer Interface)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:1000
msgid ""
"For explicit handling of files using Unicode, the standard stream codecs as "
"available through the codecs module should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:1003
msgid ""
"The codecs module should provide a short-cut open(filename,mode,encoding) "
"available which also assures that mode contains the 'b' character when "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:1009
msgid "File/Stream Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0100.rst:1011
msgid ""
"Only the user knows what encoding the input data uses, so no special magic "
"is applied.  The user will have to explicitly convert the string data to "
"Unicode objects as needed or use the file wrappers defined in the codecs "
"module (see File/Stream Output)."
msgstr ""

